<title>GREECE: Greek CPI inflation slips to 8.5 pct yr/yr in Aug.</title>
<headline>Greek CPI inflation slips to 8.5 pct yr/yr in Aug.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek consumer price inflation slipped to 8.5 percent year-on-year in August from 8.6 percent in July, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said.</p>
<p>August food prices fell by 0.2 percent month-on-month, but durable consumer goods rose by 0.3 percent and housing by 0.3 percent, it said.</p>
<p> Consumer Price Index    August 96   July 96    August 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change	0.0%	 -2.5%	   0.1%</p>
<p> Rate of change		 8.5%	  8.6%	   8.7%</p>
<p> Index (1988=100)	   281.7	 281.8	  259.6</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
